  "description": "This course provides an in-depth exploration of Computer Networks, covering the design, operation, and management of modern networking systems. Topics include the OSI and TCP/IP models; Ethernet, Wi-Fi (802.11), and fiber-optic technologies; routing protocols such as RIP, OSPF, and BGP; network security mechanisms like TLS 1.3, IPsec, and PKI; network address translation (NAT); subnetting and CIDR; Quality of Service (QoS) mechanisms; and network management protocols such as SNMP. The course also delves into wireless networking standards, cloud networking, and network virtualization technologies. Students will explore the architecture of the Internet, including DNS, HTTP/3, and TCP/IP stack operations, as well as network performance evaluation techniques using tools like Wireshark and tcpdump.",
